<title>USA: Eastbrokers to buy back 200,000 shares.</title>
<headline>Eastbrokers to buy back 200,000 shares.</headline>
<dateline>ROCKVILLE, Md. 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Eastbrokers International Inc said Monday its board had authorized the repurchase of 200,000 shares, or about $1 million worth of its stock.</p>
<p>The shares may be bought on the open market or through negotiated transactions, it said.</p>
<p>The company has 2,871,000 shares outstanding. The buyback amounts to about seven percent of its common stock, it said.</p>
<p>Eastbrokers operates a diversified investment banking and brokerage network in 12 Central and Eastern European countries.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859 1610))</p>
